Z||000000||Dseptikon2m6||05-05-2000||05:00 AM||||Would the later models (ex. 86GT's and up and/or the fastback's) front and rear fascia fit on my 85 se notchback? I like how it seems closer to the ground than my 85 notchback's pointy front fascia and also the fastback's rear fascias wrap around the exhaust tips. Thinking of buyin but wanna make sure i dont waste my money if they wont fit.||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||05-05-2000||08:01 AM||||Likely you would be better off gettin F & R from an 85 GT or 86-87 se. 1, they'd be cheaper. 2, The contour of the rear bumper would stick out away from the taillights with the fastback fascia.<BR>3, the moulded in blackstrip on the 85 is different from the 86-up.  Also remember to get inner wheel wells of the gt as the reg ones do not go all th way out.<BR>Or just keep it stock, sell it and buy what you want alredy put together by the factory.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||05-05-2000||10:47 AM||||With the exception of the moulding, all of the aero fascias are the same.  But like stimpy said, you have to get different wheel wells.  Here's what you can choose from if you don't care about the moulding:  '84 Indy, '85 GT, '85 and '86 SE, '87 SE (?), '86-'88 GT.||||reg||1
